## Tajweed Colours

Tajweed colours are **standalone constants** in `lib/ui/widgets/tajweed.dart`, used by the Tajweed Guide page (legend). The reader uses only V4 font-based tajweed; no software engine. Constants match the Madani scheme (quran.com / V4).

| Rule | Constant | Colour | Hex |
|------|----------|--------|-----|
| Silent letter | `kNotPronouncedColor()` | Grey | #9E9E9E (dark) / #BDBDBD (light) |
| Normal Madd (2 counts) | `kNormalMaadColor` | Pink | #E91E8C |
| Separated Madd (2/4/6) | `kMaadSukoonColor` | Orange | #FB8C00 |
| Connected Madd (4/5, before hamza) | `kMaadConnectedColor` | Dark Pink | #D81B60 |
| Necessary Madd (6 counts) | `kMaadLongColor` | Red | #F44336 |
| Ghunnah / Ikhfa / Idgham-gh / Iqlab / Meem | `kGhunnahColor` | Green | #43A047 |
| Qalqala (echo) | `kQalqalaColor` | Cyan | #00BCD4 |
| Tafkhim (heavy) | `kTafkhimColor` | Dark Blue | #1565C0 |

`kNotPronouncedColor(Brightness)` is the only brightness-aware colour — returns a different grey for readability on dark vs light backgrounds.
